warning[W0801]: `Food` binds a new name here — it does not test the variant `Kind.Food`
 --> mem:///main.lu:5:10
  |
1 | enum Kind { Drink, Food, Gratuity }
  |                    ---- `Food` is declared here, in `Kind`
...
5 |     for (Food, n) in [(Kind.Drink, 1)] {
  |          ^^^^ a binding, not a test
  |
  = note: a `let`, `var`, `for` or `else |…|` pattern binds every value it meets, so a bare name
    there is a new binding even when it spells a variant. To test the value, `match` on it
    (`Kind.Food => …`); to keep the binding, give it a lowercase name so it reads as one.
help: bind it under a lowercase name: `food`
  |
5 |     for (food, n) in [(Kind.Drink, 1)] {
  |
help: test the variant instead: `Kind.Food`
  |
5 |     for (Kind.Food, n) in [(Kind.Drink, 1)] {
  |
